sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-03--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-03--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-anthrobots-03: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.31" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.306"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "needs-new-data" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Basal-cell position over time is a measurable variable, and the paper states the inward-migration route as a hypothesis tied to viscosity. Public material, if any, is endpoint immunostaining, which is compatible with several rearrangements. Distinguishing inward basal migration from other polarity switches needs new live imaging or a deposited tracking set that does not exist." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Live-image basal and apical markers from the moment spheroids leave Matrigel until cilia are external, and test whether basal cells move inward rather than apical cells moving outward or new cilia differentiating in place. Inward basal migration that precedes external cilia would support the viscosity hypothesis; polarity reversal without basal displacement would refute that particular route." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Endpoint stains at day 0 and day 7 do not track which cells moved.", "Viscosity is changed by leaving the gel, which also changes adhesion and ligand presentation.", "The cell-resolution movies that would separate the routes are not deposited." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-03--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2024-anthrobots-03 by Grok 4.7: 0.68" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
